  "limitations": [
    "Single machine, single Python/Textual build; numbers are not a portable release target.",
    "capture_ms measures the capture worker only (wrapped capture_session); mount/compose overhead is excluded from it but included in startup_to_first_list_ms.",
    "publication_to_first_list_ms spans accepted capture on the UI thread to the instrumented Home rebuild that first carries every row; it is wall-clock on the shared event loop and includes worker/message scheduling.",
    "The injected-delay run demonstrates the publication-to-list interval tracks real work; the requested delay is 50.0 ms.",
    "per_cell_update_ms is the real cost of one Home state-cell update; amortized_queue_ms_per_resolved_row is the whole serial queue divided by resolved rows and is dominated by real resolution work, not a single cell update.",
    "active_navigation_ms/active_filter_ms/active_quit_ms are measured while hundreds of resolutions are still pending (the probe records pending_at_start and pending_before_quit). Navigation and quit use real Pilot key presses; the filter is driven through the Input's Changed event because Pilot's press waits for the app to drain and would outlast the queue. Navigating, filtering and the queued re-drive all leave that probe unsuitable for the why_call/group equality assertion.",
    "The superseded receipt docs/validation/u3/implementation/historical/benchmark-home-r1.json is invalid and unsafe (its sandbox was cleared after run 1, so later runs allowed absolute system roots, and its publication boundary measured a near-zero predicate check). It is preserved as history and is not relabelled valid."
